Patch 2067: DXT1/23/45 textures whose width or height is not a multiple of 4 are decoded to RGBA8 on the CPU
(BC_NATIVE=1 keeps them compressed, test only).

Windows 10's D3D12 runtime can't create block-compressed resources of such sizes (CreateCommittedResource fails,
debug-layer message 597); Windows 11 allows them, so it never failed on Windows 11 machines. J-Stars' menus use
512x78 DXT5 pieces, so on Windows 10 the menus showed without their art, entries or text. They are decoded on every
machine, so everyone sees the same image. Unaligned DXT already kept one mip level (patch 2012). This is the v0.15
installer patch 0005, which fixed a tester's Windows 10 PC, ported to v0.19. Log: [TEX] DXT ... decoded to RGBA8.

Tested on Windows 11 (US disc): main menu decodes four 512x78 textures and looks the same as with BC_NATIVE=1
(bench/fix/2026-11-10_1637-dxt2067 vs 2026-11-10_1638-dxtnative), no crash lines.

